{"type":"message","id":"e957c1ac","parentId":"99da1fcd","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:42.582Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_gGAC7aPQMTypF2PdiTOTkNBd|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9a785881918d1cf0ec4edb7acb","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/app/docs/nodes/index.md:324:- Node hosts ignore `PATH` overrides and strip dangerous startup/shell keys (`DYLD_*`, `LD_*`, `NODE_OPTIONS`, `PYTHON*`, `PERL*`, `RUBYOPT`, `SHELLOPTS`, `PS4`). If you need extra PATH entries, configure the node host service environment (or install tools in standard locations) instead of passing `PATH` via `--env`.\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:50:## CLI startup bench\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:52:Script: [`scripts/bench-cli-startup.ts`](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/scripts/bench-cli-startup.ts)\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:56:- `pnpm tsx scripts/bench-cli-startup.ts`\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:57:- `pnpm tsx scripts/bench-cli-startup.ts --runs 12`\n/app/docs/reference/test.md:58:- `pnpm tsx scripts/bench-cli-startup.ts --entry dist/entry.js --timeout-ms 45000`\n/app/docs/reference/token-use.md:21:- Workspace + bootstrap files (`AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md` when new, plus `MEMORY.md` when present or `memory.md` as a lowercase fallback). Large files are truncated by `agents.defaults.bootstrapMaxChars` (default: 20000), and total bootstrap injection is capped by `agents.defaults.bootstrapTotalMaxChars` (default: 150000). `memory/*.md` files are on-demand via memory tools and are not auto-injected.\n/app/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:14:- If BOOTSTRAP.md exists, follow its ritual and delete it once complete.\n/app/docs/reference/templates/BOOT.md:10:Add short, explicit instructions for what OpenClaw should do on startup (enable `hooks.internal.enabled`).\n/app/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md:2:title: \"BOOTSTRAP.md Template\"\n/app/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md:8:# BOOTSTRAP.md - Hello, World\n/app/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:14:If `BOOTSTRAP.md` exists, that's your birth certificate. Follow it, figure out who you are, then delete it. You won't need it again.\n/app/docs/docs.json:659:      \"source\": \"/templates/BOOTSTRAP\",\n/app/docs/docs.json:660:      \"destination\": \"/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP\"\n/app/docs/docs.json:1319:                  \"reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP\",\n/app/docs/docs.json:1904:                  \"zh-CN/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP\",\n/app/docs/providers/kilocode.md:54:OpenClaw dynamically discovers available models from the Kilo Gateway at startup. Use\n/app/docs/providers/huggingface.md:67:When you configure a Hugging Face API key (via onboarding, `HUGGINGFACE_HUB_TOKEN`, or `HF_TOKEN`), OpenClaw uses this GET to discover available chat-completion models. During **interactive onboarding**, after you enter your token you see a **Default Hugging Face model** dropdown populated from that list (or the built-in catalog if the request fails). At runtime (e.g. Gateway startup), when a key is present, OpenClaw again calls **GET** `https://router.huggingface.co/v1/models` to refresh the catalog. The list is merged with a built-in catalog (for metadata like context window and cost). If the request fails or no key is set, only the built-in catalog is used.\n/app/docs/vps.md:68:- `NODE_COMPILE_CACHE` improves repeated command startup times.\n/app/docs/vps.md:69:- `OPENCLAW_NO_RESPAWN=1` avoids extra startup overhead from a self-respawn path.\n/app/docs/vps.md:77:- Add service env for stable startup path:\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:267:- **`gateway:startup`**: After channels start and hooks are loaded\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:378:- **`session:start`**: When a new session begins\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:699:**Events**: `gateway:startup`\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:782:The gateway logs hook loading at startup:\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:788:Registered hook: boot-md -> gateway:startup\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:869:- **`src/gateway/server-startup.ts`**: Loads hooks at gateway start\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:875:Gateway startup\n/app/docs/channels/zalo.md:180:- `channels.zalo.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/twitch.md:306:- `channels.twitch.enabled` - Enable/disable channel startup\n/app/docs/channels/matrix.md:135:When E2EE is enabled, the bot will request verification from your other sessions on startup.\n/app/docs/channels/matrix.md:174:- Account startup is serialized to avoid race conditions with concurrent module imports.\n/app/docs/channels/matrix.md:221:- On startup, OpenClaw resolves room/user names in allowlists to IDs and logs the mapping; unresolved entries are ignored for allowlist matching.\n/app/docs/channels/matrix.md:280:- `channels.matrix.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:178:    - channel allowlist entries and DM allowlist entries are resolved at startup when token access allows\n/app/docs/channels/slack.md:193:    Per-channel controls (`channels.slack.channels.<id>`; names only via startup resolution or `dangerouslyAllowNameMatching`):\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:803:    Route Discord gateway WebSocket traffic and startup REST lookups (application ID + allowlist resolution) through an HTTP(S) proxy with `channels.discord.proxy`.\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:1196:- startup/auth: `enabled`, `token`, `accounts.*`, `allowBots`\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:89:  - `channels.zalouser.groups` (keys should be stable group IDs; names are resolved to IDs on startup when possible)\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:93:- On startup, OpenClaw resolves group/user names in allowlists to IDs and logs the mapping.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:303:    Telegram command menu registration is handled at startup with `setMyCommands`.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:440:    Runtime sends use the active config/secrets snapshot (startup/reload), so action paths do not perform ad-hoc SecretRef re-resolution per send.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:895:- `channels.telegram.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:958:- startup/auth: `enabled`, `botToken`, `tokenFile`, `accounts.*` (`tokenFile` must point to a regular file; symlinks are rejected)\n/app/docs/channels/broadcast-groups.md:335:- Check sandbox startup time\n/app/docs/channels/msteams.md:120:- On startup, OpenClaw resolves team/channel and user allowlist names to IDs (when Graph permissions allow)\n/app/docs/channels/troubleshooting.md:52:| `setMyCommands` rejected at startup | Inspect logs for `BOT_COMMANDS_TOO_MUCH`        | Reduce plugin/skill/custom Telegram commands or disable native menus.       |\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:180:This skips auto-spawn and the startup wait inside OpenClaw. For slow starts when auto-spawning, set `channels.signal.startupTimeoutMs`.\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:302:- `channels.signal.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/signal.md:308:- `channels.signal.startupTimeoutMs`: startup wait timeout in ms (cap 120000).\n/app/docs/channels/nextcloud-talk.md:115:- `channels.nextcloud-talk.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/channels/tlon.md:256:- `channels.tlon.enabled`: enable/disable channel startup.\n/app/docs/perplexity.md:80:If `provider: \"perplexity\"` is configured and the Perplexity key SecretRef is unresolved with no env fallback, startup/reload fails fast.\n/app/docs/install/render.mdx:95:- Deploy logs (service startup)\n/app/docs/install/northflank.mdx:51:4. **Enable MESSAGE CONTENT INTENT** under Bot → Privileged Gateway Intents (required or the bot will crash on startup)\n/app/docs/install/railway.mdx:89:4. **Enable MESSAGE CONTENT INTENT** under Bot → Privileged Gateway Intents (required or the bot will crash on startup)\n/app/docs/install/fly.md:344:If you need to change the startup command without a full redeploy:\n/app/docs/install/updating.md:72:Note: on npm installs, the gateway logs an update hint on startup (checks the current channel tag). Disable via `update.checkOnStart: false`.\n/app/docs/install/docker.md:481:`/readyz` stays ready during startup grace, then becomes `503` only if required\n/app/docs/install/docker.md:722:- Browser container startup defaults are conservative for shared/container workloads, including:\n/app/docs/install/node.md:85:  Make sure your version manager is initialized in your shell startup file (`~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`). If it isn't, `openclaw` may not be found in new terminal sessions because the PATH won't include Node's bin directory.\n/app/docs/install/node.md:109:  <Step title=\"Add it to your shell startup file\">\n/app/docs/install/index.md:195:Fix — add it to your shell startup file (`~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`):\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/openresponses-gateway.md:71:- Emit a startup warning when Chat Completions is enabled to signal legacy status.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:100:- persistent binding store with restore on startup\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:129:This avoids startup cost on every prompt and keeps cancel and reconnect semantics reliable.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:370:- backend startup/stop timeouts\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:669:- add backend health checks and startup/teardown registration\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/pty-process-supervision.md:98:### Durability and startup reconciliation\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:41:- **Persistent binding**: saved in config, reconciled on startup, intended for “named workspace” channels/topics.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:308:  - on startup: load configured top-level `type: \"acp\"` bindings, ensure ACP sessions exist, ensure bindings exist.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:339:- Better diagnostics (`/acp status`, startup reconciliation logs).\n/app/docs/web/index.md:103:  explicitly (full origins). Without it, gateway startup is refused by default.\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:198:### Speed up CLI startup (module compile cache)\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:215:- `OPENCLAW_NO_RESPAWN=1` avoids extra startup cost from CLI self-respawn.\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:218:### systemd startup tuning (optional)\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:221:jitter and keep startup env stable:\n/app/docs/platforms/windows.md:54:If you do want managed startup on native Windows:\n/app/docs/platforms/windows.md:131:### Verify startup chain\n/app/docs/platforms/digitalocean.md:44:Use a clean base image (Ubuntu 24.04 LTS). Avoid third-party Marketplace 1-click images unless you have reviewed their startup scripts and firewall defaults.\n/app/docs/help/debugging.md:57:  workspace** when missing (and skip BOOTSTRAP.md).\n/app/docs/help/debugging.md:79:   - Sets `agent.skipBootstrap=true` (no BOOTSTRAP.md).\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1189:4. Start a new session so the skills snapshot refreshes.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1461:OpenClaw enforces token auth by default, including loopback. If no token is configured, gateway startup auto-generates one and saves it to `gateway.auth.token`, so **local WS clients must authenticate**. This blocks other local processes from calling the Gateway.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1854:transcripts - it just starts a new session.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2401:Fix: OpenClaw now strips unsigned thinking blocks for Google Antigravity Claude. If it still appears, start a **new session** or set `/thinking off` for that agent.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2496:OpenClaw enforces a runtime lock by binding the WebSocket listener immediately on startup (default `ws://127.0.0.1:18789`). If the bind fails with `EADDRINUSE`, it throws `GatewayLockError` indicating another instance is already listening.\n/app/docs/help/testing.md:66:  - Uses Vitest `vmForks` for faster file startup.\n/app/docs/debug/node-issue.md:13:Running OpenClaw via Node with `tsx` fails at startup with:\n/app/docs/start/hubs.md:173:- [Templates: BOOTSTRAP](/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP)\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:74:By default, OpenClaw uses `~/.openclaw/workspace` as the agent workspace, and will create it (plus starter `AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`) automatically on setup/first agent run. `BOOTSTRAP.md` is only created when the workspace is brand new (it should not come back after you delete it). `MEMORY.md` is optional (not auto-created); when present, it is loaded for normal sessions. Subagent sessions only inject `AGENTS.md` and `TOOLS.md`.\n/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md:22:- Seeds `AGENTS.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`.\n/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md:25:- Removes `BOOTSTRAP.md` when finished so it only runs once.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:54:- Web tool SecretRefs are resolved atomically at gateway startup/reload.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:56:- If the selected provider SecretRef is unresolved and no provider env fallback exists, startup/reload fails fast.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:379:- If Firecrawl is active and its SecretRef is unresolved with no `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` fallback, startup/reload fails fast.\n/app/docs/tools/skills.md:244:OpenClaw snapshots the eligible skills **when a session starts** and reuses that list for subsequent turns in the same session. Changes to skills or config take effect on the next new session.\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:132:At startup, OpenClaw does roughly this:\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:169:These caches reduce bursty startup and repeated command overhead. They are safe\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:313:  bursty startup/reload work."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":23,"aggregated":"/app/docs/nodes/index.md:324:- Node hosts ignore `PATH` overrides and