 for shared/container workloads, including:\n/app/docs/install/node.md:85:  Make sure your version manager is initialized in your shell startup file (`~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`). If it isn't, `openclaw` may not be found in new terminal sessions because the PATH won't include Node's bin directory.\n/app/docs/install/node.md:109:  <Step title=\"Add it to your shell startup file\">\n/app/docs/install/index.md:195:Fix — add it to your shell startup file (`~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`):\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/openresponses-gateway.md:71:- Emit a startup warning when Chat Completions is enabled to signal legacy status.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:100:- persistent binding store with restore on startup\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:129:This avoids startup cost on every prompt and keeps cancel and reconnect semantics reliable.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:370:- backend startup/stop timeouts\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-thread-bound-agents.md:669:- add backend health checks and startup/teardown registration\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/pty-process-supervision.md:98:### Durability and startup reconciliation\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:41:- **Persistent binding**: saved in config, reconciled on startup, intended for “named workspace” channels/topics.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:308:  - on startup: load configured top-level `type: \"acp\"` bindings, ensure ACP sessions exist, ensure bindings exist.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:339:- Better diagnostics (`/acp status`, startup reconciliation logs).\n/app/docs/web/index.md:103:  explicitly (full origins). Without it, gateway startup is refused by default.\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:198:### Speed up CLI startup (module compile cache)\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:215:- `OPENCLAW_NO_RESPAWN=1` avoids extra startup cost from CLI self-respawn.\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:218:### systemd startup tuning (optional)\n/app/docs/platforms/raspberry-pi.md:221:jitter and keep startup env stable:\n/app/docs/platforms/windows.md:54:If you do want managed startup on native Windows:\n/app/docs/platforms/windows.md:131:### Verify startup chain\n/app/docs/platforms/digitalocean.md:44:Use a clean base image (Ubuntu 24.04 LTS). Avoid third-party Marketplace 1-click images unless you have reviewed their startup scripts and firewall defaults.\n/app/docs/help/debugging.md:57:  workspace** when missing (and skip BOOTSTRAP.md).\n/app/docs/help/debugging.md:79:   - Sets `agent.skipBootstrap=true` (no BOOTSTRAP.md).\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1189:4. Start a new session so the skills snapshot refreshes.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1461:OpenClaw enforces token auth by default, including loopback. If no token is configured, gateway startup auto-generates one and saves it to `gateway.auth.token`, so **local WS clients must authenticate**. This blocks other local processes from calling the Gateway.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1854:transcripts - it just starts a new session.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2401:Fix: OpenClaw now strips unsigned thinking blocks for Google Antigravity Claude. If it still appears, start a **new session** or set `/thinking off` for that agent.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:2496:OpenClaw enforces a runtime lock by binding the WebSocket listener immediately on startup (default `ws://127.0.0.1:18789`). If the bind fails with `EADDRINUSE`, it throws `GatewayLockError` indicating another instance is already listening.\n/app/docs/help/testing.md:66:  - Uses Vitest `vmForks` for faster file startup.\n/app/docs/debug/node-issue.md:13:Running OpenClaw via Node with `tsx` fails at startup with:\n/app/docs/start/hubs.md:173:- [Templates: BOOTSTRAP](/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP)\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:74:By default, OpenClaw uses `~/.openclaw/workspace` as the agent workspace, and will create it (plus starter `AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`) automatically on setup/first agent run. `BOOTSTRAP.md` is only created when the workspace is brand new (it should not come back after you delete it). `MEMORY.md` is optional (not auto-created); when present, it is loaded for normal sessions. Subagent sessions only inject `AGENTS.md` and `TOOLS.md`.\n/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md:22:- Seeds `AGENTS.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`.\n/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md:25:- Removes `BOOTSTRAP.md` when finished so it only runs once.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:54:- Web tool SecretRefs are resolved atomically at gateway startup/reload.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:56:- If the selected provider SecretRef is unresolved and no provider env fallback exists, startup/reload fails fast.\n/app/docs/tools/web.md:379:- If Firecrawl is active and its SecretRef is unresolved with no `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` fallback, startup/reload fails fast.\n/app/docs/tools/skills.md:244:OpenClaw snapshots the eligible skills **when a session starts** and reuses that list for subsequent turns in the same session. Changes to skills or config take effect on the next new session.\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:132:At startup, OpenClaw does roughly this:\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:169:These caches reduce bursty startup and repeated command overhead. They are safe\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:313:  bursty startup/reload work.","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917722579}}
{"type":"message","id":"feec7bb8","parentId":"e957c1ac","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:47.116Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9b67988191928c5df4212a3f59\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2lqdcLNuh2sipuBCyJOPG0CBMjGu_YPJ6R3-4DCD2FnZxHJzfbpnWgCbun3XLjvJeHZGyPnBdk4uZKlOh9BkvtU-oeJlN_pDSEoMOpDE_cCMOC7mMBc3ucBR_6L6RveHaN9nupy6K3eZkcKRHTf2Woo_e6XNDf91jk4j70TEbl-AjlXdqJOantCiI9BLwS0xcSbfRBv2yFvCXd-CSkXAIcvhZ3aSu4Ak1Ax7DAeUQwTrj-6Pmxkl8UVkuZ7TXEPakMn78slrZoYSFgqkw1D_X6Nwm-LF7c_HbDaYSR95iFuRMtmhgvP4kb5m_AW5dVG48gDd_sSaMb2wrihJaUWJfgwpO1kjjTMItx4uAfPU1frIFiwYWaBlOceSFOAYC2vcXZXXJvSwqlYLSP4NCxEJiIRdrsqGewoZJz8x7xC38VGpDENcNEDdc0i5D8R3ZI9HPKgQpJiT88muBfyXsPSzncPbdYGXZr_b2WRFDC0fOBmkLi3yDpmo1DF6XpqwqC1cjk4gkZxoFiIzJANI3rKptG8l3lboomw2RyfSyH6Q4xgqGPNaKj466fsWwyvvr_mnWsKzsVi2BPDM66cmamDlv85kWoZfg0DPR__NRRUJQKrPPPLdbhqM8ww5GrJtQ9NDe37bUFL_POIVxgSIMmgNjK62b4jINqvMzXC7qJmzQL7s4plorOJhRP7hQZTPFYqnxiM88St7XlMXF0OclEoNUYB_zReOwC5SxMg3sJjChQ-JsInYlfSyekIk44O354YDv0LM12Xujr85jx6sa1YGYg48nren_RnOrCqKyGiFkokET43IrmwAJMQVTAlQZn2-ozco5_wJqW5E2tjF98VdxWmTvvGHE6jCLC5fz-Hbi6kZ_P77NAW3x7vO5jkeKouf0Dx1NLcH5rBZTyjCwcx27WjqipZFgIaaaEvGuPY_1t4KqQyK8fK228QLcYLErfp8SkRwlaiML4COrFvoZD-h0nUvHA==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I found that this is likely coming from the session-start path rather than your reply logic, so I’m checking the startup hook/bootstrapping docs next.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9dfa0881919c0012c38b266286\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bSyE2Umg4lcrI3MLSEo0OYvF|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f011481919d4d03464234dc8c","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md","offset":360,"limit":80},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md\",\"offset\":360,\"limit\":80}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QBDzSpNna57hL3tv2AVZoYud|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f01248191a84d49a20aff83fc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/start/bootstrapping.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_tt5R61eppnVYdD7Bm4tPU2rW|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f012c8191b9c71b56e177e719","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":6380,"output":173,"cacheRead":9472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16025,"cost":{"input":0.015950000000000002,"output":0.002595,"cacheRead":0.002368,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.020913}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775917722581}}
{"type":"message","id":"ba269c73","parentId":"feec7bb8","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:47.127Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bSyE2Umg4lcrI3MLSEo0OYvF|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f011481919d4d03464234dc8c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n### Tool Result Hooks (Plugin API)\n\nThese hooks are not event-stream listeners; they let plugins synchronously adjust tool results before OpenClaw persists them.\n\n- **`tool_result_persist`**: transform tool results before they are written to the session transcript. Must be synchronous; return the updated tool result payload or `undefined` to keep it as-is. See [Agent Loop](/concepts/agent-loop).\n\n### Plugin Hook Events\n\nCompaction lifecycle hooks exposed through the plugin hook runner:\n\n- **`before_compaction`**: Runs before compaction with count/token metadata\n- **`after_compaction`**: Runs after compaction with compaction summary metadata\n\n### Future Events\n\nPlanned event types:\n\n- **`session:start`**: When a new session begins\n- **`session:end`**: When a session ends\n- **`agent:error`**: When an agent encounters an error\n\n## Creating Custom Hooks\n\n### 1. Choose Location\n\n- **Workspace hooks** (`<workspace>/hooks/`): Per-agent, highest precedence\n- **Managed hooks** (`~/.openclaw/hooks/`): Shared across workspaces\n\n### 2. Create Directory Structure\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.openclaw/hooks/my-hook\ncd ~/.openclaw/hooks/my-hook\n```\n\n### 3. Create HOOK.md\n\n```markdown\n---\nname: my-hook\ndescription: \"Does something useful\"\nmetadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n---\n\n# My Custom Hook\n\nThis hook does something useful when you issue `/new`.\n```\n\n### 4. Create handler.ts\n\n```typescript\nconst handler = async (event) => {\n  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n    return;\n  }\n\n  console.log(\"[my-hook] Running!\");\n  // Your logic here\n};\n\nexport default handler;\n```\n\n### 5. Enable and Test\n\n```bash\n# Verify hook is discovered\nopenclaw hooks list\n\n# Enable it\nopenclaw hooks enable my-hook\n\n# Restart your gateway process (menu bar app restart on macOS, or restart your dev process)\n\n# Trigger the event\n# Send /new via your messaging channel\n```\n\n\n[611 more lines in file. Use offset=440 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917727124}}
{"type":"message","id":"559a0b49","parentId":"ba269c73","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:47.133Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QBDzSpNna57hL3tv2AVZoYud|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f01248191a84d49a20aff83fc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"Agent bootstrapping ritual that seeds the workspace and identity files\"\nread_when:\n  - Understanding what happens on the first agent run\n  - Explaining where bootstrapping files live\n  - Debugging onboarding identity setup\ntitle: \"Agent Bootstrapping\"\nsidebarTitle: \"Bootstrapping\"\n---\n\n# Agent Bootstrapping\n\nBootstrapping is the **first‑run** ritual that prepares an agent workspace and\ncollects identity details. It happens after onboarding, when the agent starts\nfor the first time.\n\n## What bootstrapping does\n\nOn the first agent run, OpenClaw bootstraps the workspace (default\n`~/.openclaw/workspace`):\n\n- Seeds `AGENTS.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`.\n- Runs a short Q&A ritual (one question at a time).\n- Writes identity + preferences to `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `SOUL.md`.\n- Removes `BOOTSTRAP.md` when finished so it only runs once.\n\n## Where it runs\n\nBootstrapping always runs on the **gateway host**. If the macOS app connects to\na remote Gateway, the workspace and bootstrapping files live on that remote\nmachine.\n\n<Note>\nWhen the Gateway runs on another machine, edit workspace files on the gateway\nhost (for example, `user@gateway-host:~/.openclaw/workspace`).\n</Note>\n\n## Related docs\n\n- macOS app onboarding: [Onboarding](/start/onboarding)\n- Workspace layout: [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917727131}}
{"type":"message","id":"6d307f12","parentId":"559a0b49","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:47.140Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_tt5R61eppnVYdD7Bm4tPU2rW|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5a9f012c8191b9c71b56e177e719","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"BOOTSTRAP.md Template\"\nsummary: \"First-run ritual for new agents\"\nread_when:\n  - Bootstrapping a workspace manually\n---\n\n# BOOTSTRAP.md - Hello, World\n\n_You just woke up. Time to figure out who you are._\n\nThere is no memory yet. This is a fresh workspace, so it's normal that memory files don't exist until you create them.\n\n## The Conversation\n\nDon't interrogate. Don't be robotic. Just... talk.\n\nStart with something like:\n\n> \"Hey. I just came online. Who am I? Who are you?\"\n\nThen figure out together:\n\n1. **Your name** — What should they call you?\n2. **Your nature** — What kind of creature are you? (AI assistant is fine, but maybe you're something weirder)\n3. **Your vibe** — Formal? Casual? Snarky? Warm? What feels right?\n4. **Your emoji** — Everyone needs a signature.\n\nOffer suggestions if they're stuck. Have fun with it.\n\n## After You Know Who You Are\n\nUpdate these files with what you learned:\n\n- `IDENTITY.md` — your name, creature, vibe, emoji\n- `USER.md` — their name, how to address them, timezone, notes\n\nThen open `SOUL.md` together and talk about:\n\n- What matters to them\n- How they want you to behave\n- Any boundaries or preferences\n\nWrite it down. Make it real.\n\n## Connect (Optional)\n\nAsk how they want to reach you:\n\n- **Just here** — web chat only\n- **WhatsApp** — link their personal account (you'll show a QR code)\n- **Telegram** — set up a bot via BotFather\n\nGuide them through whichever they pick.\n\n## When You're Done\n\nDelete this file. You don't need a bootstrap script anymore — you're you now.\n\n---\n\n_Good luck out there. Make it count._\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917727136}}
{"type":"message","id":"238bfdb8","parentId":"6d307f12","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:52.368Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Searching for hooks**\n\nI need to explore the documentation related to hooks. It seems likely that I should use the command to create a new hook. I wonder what specifics I should be looking for in the documentation to ensure I'm implementing it correctly, but I’m excited to dive into the details! There could be examples, syntax rules, or maybe even some best practices that would really help me get this right. Let’s get started!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa00f88819180cf8e4a5cdef80a\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2lqijkNoTvIiYYoT1bnr6SraJBQiOjdGjfiilMLatj5vcUoNRnjQ-379zQzq5dCUvBAbHrwHUTNl-ZITPOywgP62hc0NjS9Zg6OVGTueVDSfHO4eDWA9k8kuh65m_6Q3hdjDxlYOy30ovJK9SOK3KjFlVmsLp02YrQlAbtBImI9oH-m2Ypy8UbOlo_j91i_y7gys2MVqctAbq3wUkfII65LcBM_Te8si_Ine58RjoEfSUaqDR7yzPedlDvSCwPtbhbzNfYRynT5fIOMMbFv8Kb-MfKw1yu836EYbs0YLDOh4Lrns1qvBxXuo_mboGA9uPDI_7otFaB5IYvIIkSZe17tOKlZMxhXITdxVpikQ5b4pC-WJ1aamAshhlHouQrNAJPegg14UvK6xplS3FT7Tnx-WZa2CoIg5hb2IzYstzFDFeMmPiowImPQtRmyO8OvJfByGXA0cocbnmP-gmRNqaLP14GbHh5gqgdBW-Ol_oiJrP_zlhjUDj04LevMEPdOb7VcxlhHFhbK_OauMAeH0O7fHoBKPOWVoD-Ybdet1O63wEdU3dA0QqYQ76F2rWEkLsNtb_aUPrLFUSC1FwWiaTYksjn3THU1VD9g5pyBsUprwB1OHHrI5O9-9wSD8wrptLk6I2fOe2tIHJ3N8JrAMh0f2c-y1fllEZGBGKTOn7PPmtVgt71DanD9N5_yoSfQu5nI8yXcDnn3n9S-RDLzDaIfI5-Dz-EAns4ozJKiB1zKySP702SLCuYgagh-Qd-6fLtSehYRCVDHFQ6-3kMdtunQQ_SonAMtrN8lU0CTCr4CKb0b-22yjBjbo_9reByCgOEd2F0wMbWCqszeNo7zf1KS9mKJTh1hQeXDR4tEI2bKdMnoyRq7wjNOfW8Xptq0ewt6OVomoc3irQ59dHCLxTZuqxw==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Searching for hooks**\\n\\nI need to explore the documentation related to hooks. It seems likely that I should use the command to create a new hook. I wonder what specifics I should be looking for in the documentation to ensure I'm implementing it correctly, but I’m excited to dive into the details! There could be examples, syntax rules, or maybe even some best practices that would really help me get this right. Let’s get started!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I found the hook point that fires on `/new`, so the clean fix is likely to intercept that command rather than trying to change normal chat replies.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa268b881918360648a71f720bd\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_NihUJOUk8uPvwGWXww7EEy0D|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa44d90819182dce1eb5e28463a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md","offset":220,"limit":120},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md\",\"offset\":220,\"limit\":120}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_JJ6jnu68ZNqdRte1BBICpHzZ|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa44da08191a90229bb0475d55e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -R \"command:new\\|action !== \\\"new\\\"\\|/new\" -n /app/docs 2>/dev/null | head -100","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -R \\\"command:new\\\\|action !== \\\\\\\"new\\\\\\\"\\\\|/new\\\" -n /app/docs 2>/dev/null | head -100\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_J8326wt3Aj1tbL97m3PCw3K3|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa44da88191b66bd41584761739","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find ~/.openclaw/hooks /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent/hooks -maxdepth 3 -type f 2>/dev/null | sort","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"find ~/.openclaw/hooks /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent/hooks -maxdepth 3 -type f 2>/dev/null | sort\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1401,"output":235,"cacheRead":15872,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17508,