{"type":"message","id":"d1c78498","parentId":"238bfdb8","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:52.385Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_NihUJOUk8uPvwGWXww7EEy0D|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa44d90819182dce1eb5e28463a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"  context: {\n    // Command events:\n    sessionEntry?: SessionEntry,\n    sessionId?: string,\n    sessionFile?: string,\n    commandSource?: string,    // e.g., 'whatsapp', 'telegram'\n    senderId?: string,\n    workspaceDir?: string,\n    bootstrapFiles?: WorkspaceBootstrapFile[],\n    cfg?: OpenClawConfig,\n    // Message events (see Message Events section for full details):\n    from?: string,             // message:received\n    to?: string,               // message:sent\n    content?: string,\n    channelId?: string,\n    success?: boolean,         // message:sent\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Event Types\n\n### Command Events\n\nTriggered when agent commands are issued:\n\n- **`command`**: All command events (general listener)\n- **`command:new`**: When `/new` command is issued\n- **`command:reset`**: When `/reset` command is issued\n- **`command:stop`**: When `/stop` command is issued\n\n### Session Events\n\n- **`session:compact:before`**: Right before compaction summarizes history\n- **`session:compact:after`**: After compaction completes with summary metadata\n\nInternal hook payloads emit these as `type: \"session\"` with `action: \"compact:before\"` / `action: \"compact:after\"`; listeners subscribe with the combined keys above.\nSpecific handler registration uses the literal key format `${type}:${action}`. For these events, register `session:compact:before` and `session:compact:after`.\n\n### Agent Events\n\n- **`agent:bootstrap`**: Before workspace bootstrap files are injected (hooks may mutate `context.bootstrapFiles`)\n\n### Gateway Events\n\nTriggered when the gateway starts:\n\n- **`gateway:startup`**: After channels start and hooks are loaded\n\n### Message Events\n\nTriggered when messages are received or sent:\n\n- **`message`**: All message events (general listener)\n- **`message:received`**: When an inbound message is received from any channel. Fires early in processing before media understanding. Content may contain raw placeholders like `<media:audio>` for media attachments that haven't been processed yet.\n- **`message:transcribed`**: When a message has been fully processed, including audio transcription and link understanding. At this point, `transcript` contains the full transcript text for audio messages. Use this hook when you need access to transcribed audio content.\n- **`message:preprocessed`**: Fires for every message after all media + link understanding completes, giving hooks access to the fully enriched body (transcripts, image descriptions, link summaries) before the agent sees it.\n- **`message:sent`**: When an outbound message is successfully sent\n\n#### Message Event Context\n\nMessage events include rich context about the message:\n\n```typescript\n// message:received context\n{\n  from: string,           // Sender identifier (phone number, user ID, etc.)\n  content: string,        // Message content\n  timestamp?: number,     // Unix timestamp when received\n  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"whatsapp\", \"telegram\", \"discord\")\n  accountId?: string,     // Provider account ID for multi-account setups\n  conversationId?: string, // Chat/conversation ID\n  messageId?: string,     // Message ID from the provider\n  metadata?: {            // Additional provider-specific data\n    to?: string,\n    provider?: string,\n    surface?: string,\n    threadId?: string,\n    senderId?: string,\n    senderName?: string,\n    senderUsername?: string,\n    senderE164?: string,\n  }\n}\n\n// message:sent context\n{\n  to: string,             // Recipient identifier\n  content: string,        // Message content that was sent\n  success: boolean,       // Whether the send succeeded\n  error?: string,         // Error message if sending failed\n  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"whatsapp\", \"telegram\", \"discord\")\n  accountId?: string,     // Provider account ID\n  conversationId?: string, // Chat/conversation ID\n  messageId?: string,     // Message ID returned by the provider\n  isGroup?: boolean,      // Whether this outbound message belongs to a group/channel context\n  groupId?: string,       // Group/channel identifier for correlation with message:received\n}\n\n// message:transcribed context\n{\n  body?: string,          // Raw inbound body before enrichment\n  bodyForAgent?: string,  // Enriched body visible to the agent\n  transcript: string,     // Audio transcript text\n  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"telegram\", \"whatsapp\")\n  conversationId?: string,\n  messageId?: string,\n}\n\n// message:preprocessed context\n{\n  body?: string,          // Raw inbound body\n  bodyForAgent?: string,  // Final enriched body after media/link understanding\n  transcript?: string,    // Transcript when audio was present\n  channelId: string,      // Channel (e.g., \"telegram\", \"whatsapp\")\n  conversationId?: string,\n  messageId?: string,\n  isGroup?: boolean,\n  groupId?: string,\n}\n\n[711 more lines in file. Use offset=340 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917732375}}
{"type":"message","id":"a9df94b0","parentId":"d1c78498","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:52.407Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_JJ6jnu68ZNqdRte1BBICpHzZ|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa44da08191a90229bb0475d55e","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/app/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:128:- **Reset** (`/new`, `/reset`) creates a new `sessionId` for that `sessionKey`.\n/app/docs/providers/huggingface.md:20:1. Create a fine-grained token at [Hugging Face → Settings → Tokens](https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens/new?ownUserPermissions=inference.serverless.write&tokenType=fineGrained) with the **Make calls to Inference Providers** permission.\n/app/docs/providers/minimax.md:15:Source: [MiniMax M2.5 release note](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m25)\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:4:  - You want event-driven automation for /new, /reset, /stop, and agent lifecycle events\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:17:- **Hooks** (this page): run inside the Gateway when agent events fire, like `/new`, `/reset`, `/stop`, or lifecycle events.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:35:- Save session context to memory when `/new` is issued\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:46:- **💾 session-memory**: Saves session context to your agent workspace (default `~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/`) when you issue `/new`\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:146:  { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🔗\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"], \"requires\": { \"bins\": [\"node\"] } } }\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:155:- Listens for `/new` commands\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:173:- **`events`**: Array of events to listen for (e.g., `[\"command:new\", \"command:reset\"]`)\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:192:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:247:- **`command:new`**: When `/new` command is issued\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:402:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:407:This hook does something useful when you issue `/new`.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:414:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:437:# Send /new via your messaging channel\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:508:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:574:Saves session context to memory when you issue `/new`.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:576:**Events**: `command:new`\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:756:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:769:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } } # Specific\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:785:Registered hook: session-memory -> command:new\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:891:User sends /new\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:982:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:1006:   metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:647:    - `/focus <target>` bind current/new thread to a subagent/session target\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:747:    - In a bound channel or thread, `/new` and `/reset` reset the same ACP session in place.\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:97:- Sender checks apply to both normal group messages and control commands (for example `/new`, `/reset`).\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:121:- Authorized control commands (for example `/new`) can bypass mention gating.\n/app/docs/channels/feishu.md:375:In addition to allowing the group itself, **all messages** in that group are gated by the sender open_id: only users listed in `groups.<chat_id>.allowFrom` have their messages processed; messages from other members are ignored (this is full sender-level gating, not only for control commands like /reset or /new).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:30:    Run `/newbot`, follow prompts, and save the token.\n/app/docs/channels/group-messages.md:70:4. Session-level directives (`/verbose on`, `/think high`, `/new` or `/reset`, `/compact`) apply only to that group’s session; send them as standalone messages so they register. Your personal DM session remains independent.\n/app/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:328:  - If a direct handle does not have an existing DM chat, OpenClaw will create one via `POST /api/v1/chat/new`. This requires the BlueBubbles Private API to be enabled.\n/app/docs/install/northflank.mdx:42:2. Run `/newbot`\n/app/docs/install/railway.mdx:80:2. Run `/newbot`\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:26:- Keep `/acp`, `/new`, `/reset`, `/focus`, and delivery behavior consistent across Discord and Telegram.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:51:- In bound conversations, `/new` and `/reset` reset the bound ACP session in place and keep the binding attached.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:334:- Align `/acp`, `/new`, `/reset`, and `/focus` behavior in bound Telegram/Discord conversations.\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:24:Today we have command-specific checks (for example `/new` and `/reset`) that\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:44:`/new` and `/reset` would use `bound_acp_or_owner_or_allowlist`.\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:77:3. Move `/new` and `/reset` to metadata-driven policy.\n/app/docs/web/tui.md:105:- `/new` or `/reset` (reset the session)\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:129:  - [Do sessions reset automatically if I never send `/new`?](#do-sessions-reset-automatically-if-i-never-send-new)\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1848:Send `/new` or `/reset` as a standalone message. See [Session management](/concepts/session).\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1884:- Use `/compact` before long tasks, and `/new` when switching topics.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1930:  /new\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1947:Fix: start a fresh session with `/new` (standalone message).\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:141:    resetTriggers: [\"/new\", \"/reset\"],\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:155:- `/new` or `/reset` starts a fresh session for that chat (configurable via `resetTriggers`). If sent alone, the agent replies with a short hello to confirm the reset.\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:707:    \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:713:      description: \"Runs when /new is invoked\",\n/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:103:- `/reset` or `/new [model]` (optional model hint; remainder is passed through)\n/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:124:- `/new <model>` accepts a model alias, `provider/model`, or a provider name (fuzzy match); if no match, the text is treated as the message body.\n/app/docs/tools/acp-agents.md:209:- In bound conversations, `/new` and `/reset` reset the same ACP session key in place.\n/app/docs/zh-CN/reference/session-management-compaction.md:97:- **重置**（`/new`、`/reset`）为该 `sessionKey` 创建一个新的 `sessionId`。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/providers/minimax.md:20:来源：[MiniMax M2.1 发布说明](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m21)\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:3:  - 你想为 /new、/reset、/stop 和智能体生命周期事件实现事件驱动自动化\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:24:- **Hooks**（本页）：当智能体事件触发时在 Gateway 网关内运行，如 `/new`、`/reset`、`/stop` 或生命周期事件。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:42:- 在发出 `/new` 时将会话上下文保存到记忆\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:53:- **💾 session-memory**：当你发出 `/new` 时将会话上下文保存到智能体工作区（默认 `~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/`）\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:138:  { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🔗\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"], \"requires\": { \"bins\": [\"node\"] } } }\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:147:- Listens for `/new` commands\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:165:- **`events`**：要监听的事件数组（例如 `[\"command:new\", \"command:reset\"]`）\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:186:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:234:- **`command:new`**：当发出 `/new` 命令时\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:284:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:289:This hook does something useful when you issue `/new`.\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:298:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:321:# Send /new via your messaging channel\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:392:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:456:当你发出 `/new` 时将会话上下文保存到记忆。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:458:**事件**：`command:new`\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:597:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:610:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } } # Specific\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:626:Registered hook: session-memory -> command:new\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:727:用户发送 /new\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:816:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/zh-CN/automation/hooks.md:840:   metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/zh-CN/channels/feishu.md:377:除群组白名单外，该群组内**所有消息**均按发送者 open_id 校验：仅 `groups.<chat_id>.allowFrom` 中列出的用户消息会被处理，其他成员的消息会被忽略（此为发送者级白名单，不仅针对 /reset、/new 等控制命令）。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/channels/telegram.md:54:2. 运行 `/newbot`，然后按照提示操作（名称 + 以 `bot` 结尾的用户名）。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/channels/telegram.md:92:- `/newbot` 创建机器人并返回 token（请保密）。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/channels/group-messages.md:77:4. 会话级指令（`/verbose on`、`/think high`、`/new` 或 `/reset`、`/compact`）仅适用于该群组的会话；将它们作为独立消息发送以使其生效。你的个人私信会话保持独立。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/channels/bluebubbles.md:252:  - 如果直接句柄没有现有的私信聊天，OpenClaw 将通过 `POST /api/v1/chat/new` 创建一个。这需要启用 BlueBubbles Private API。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/install/northflank.mdx:49:2. 运行 `/newbot`\n/app/docs/zh-CN/install/railway.mdx:87:2. 执行 `/newbot`\n/app/docs/zh-CN/web/tui.md:111:- `/new` 或 `/reset`（重置会话）\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:131:  - [如果我从不发送 `/new`，会话会自动重置吗？](#do-sessions-reset-automatically-if-i-never-send-new)\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:1579:发送 `/new` 或 `/reset` 作为独立消息。参阅[会话管理](/concepts/session)。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:1581:### 如果我从不发送 /new，会话会自动重置吗\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:1608:- 在长任务之前使用 `/compact`，切换话题时使用 `/new`。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:1653:  /new\n/app/docs/zh-CN/help/faq.md:1668:修复：使用 `/new`（独立消息）开始新会话。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/start/openclaw.md:174:    resetTriggers: [\"/new\", \"/reset\"],\n/app/docs/zh-CN/start/openclaw.md:188:- `/new` 或 `/reset` 为该聊天启动新会话（可通过 `resetTriggers` 配置）。如果单独发送，智能体会回复一个简短的问候来确认重置。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:92:- `/reset` 或 `/new [model]`（可选模型提示；其余部分传递）\n/app/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:112:- `/new <model>` 接受模型别名、`provider/model` 或提供商名称（模糊匹配）；如果没有匹配，文本被视为消息正文。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:231:- **模型选择很重要：** 旧版/传统模型可能对提示词注入和工具滥用的抵抗力较弱。对于任何带有工具的机器人，优先使用现代的、经过指令强化的模型。我们推荐 Anthropic Opus 4.5，因为它在识别提示词注入方面相当出色（参见[\"安全性的进步\"](https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-4-5)）。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/gateway/troubleshooting.md:387:**检查 3：** 是否有人发送了 `/new`、`/reset` 或重置触发器？\n/app/docs/zh-CN/gateway/configuration.md:975:- 控制命令（例如 `/queue`、`/new`）绕过防抖，保持独立。\n/app/docs/zh-CN/gateway/configuration.md:2695:    resetTriggers: [\"/new\", \"/reset\"],"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":25,"aggregated":"/app/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:128:- **Reset** (`/new`, `/reset`) creates a new `sessionId` for that `sessionKey`.\n/app/docs/providers/huggingface.md:20:1. Create a fine-grained token at [Hugging Face → Settings → Tokens](https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens/new?ownUserPermissions=inference.serverless.write&tokenType=fineGrained) with the **Make calls to Inference Providers** permission.\n/app/docs/providers/minimax.md:15:Source: [MiniMax M2.5 release note](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m25)\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:4:  - You want event-driven automation for /new, /reset, /stop, and agent lifecycle events\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:17:- **Hooks** (this page): run inside the Gateway when agent events fire, like `/new`, `/reset`, `/stop`, or lifecycle events.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:35:- Save session context to memory when `/new` is issued\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:46:- **💾 session-memory**: Saves session context to your agent workspace (default `~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/`) when you issue `/new`\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:146:  { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🔗\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"], \"requires\": { \"bins\": [\"node\"] } } }\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:155:- Listens for `/new` commands\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:173:- **`events`**: Array of events to listen for (e.g., `[\"command:new\", \"command:reset\"]`)\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:192:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:247:- **`command:new`**: When `/new` command is issued\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:402:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:407:This hook does something useful when you issue `/new`.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:414:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:437:# Send /new via your messaging channel\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:508:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:574:Saves session context to memory when you issue `/new`.\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:576:**Events**: `command:new`\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:756:  if (event.type !== \"command\" || event.action !== \"new\") {\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:769:metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } } # Specific\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:785:Registered hook: session-memory -> command:new\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:891:User sends /new\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:982:          \"event\": \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/automation/hooks.md:1006:   metadata: { \"openclaw\": { \"emoji\": \"🎯\", \"events\": [\"command:new\"] } }\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:647:    - `/focus <target>` bind current/new thread to a subagent/session target\n/app/docs/channels/discord.md:747:    - In a bound channel or thread, `/new` and `/reset` reset the same ACP session in place.\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:97:- Sender checks apply to both normal group messages and control commands (for example `/new`, `/reset`).\n/app/docs/channels/zalouser.md:121:- Authorized control commands (for example `/new`) can bypass mention gating.\n/app/docs/channels/feishu.md:375:In addition to allowing the group itself, **all messages** in that group are gated by the sender open_id: only users listed in `groups.<chat_id>.allowFrom` have their messages processed; messages from other members are ignored (this is full sender-level gating, not only for control commands like /reset or /new).\n/app/docs/channels/telegram.md:30:    Run `/newbot`, follow prompts, and save the token.\n/app/docs/channels/group-messages.md:70:4. Session-level directives (`/verbose on`, `/think high`, `/new` or `/reset`, `/compact`) apply only to that group’s session; send them as standalone messages so they register. Your personal DM session remains independent.\n/app/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:328:  - If a direct handle does not have an existing DM chat, OpenClaw will create one via `POST /api/v1/chat/new`. This requires the BlueBubbles Private API to be enabled.\n/app/docs/install/northflank.mdx:42:2. Run `/newbot`\n/app/docs/install/railway.mdx:80:2. Run `/newbot`\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:26:- Keep `/acp`, `/new`, `/reset`, `/focus`, and delivery behavior consistent across Discord and Telegram.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:51:- In bound conversations, `/new` and `/reset` reset the bound ACP session in place and keep the binding attached.\n/app/docs/experiments/plans/acp-persistent-bindings-discord-channels-telegram-topics.md:334:- Align `/acp`, `/new`, `/reset`, and `/focus` behavior in bound Telegram/Discord conversations.\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:24:Today we have command-specific checks (for example `/new` and `/reset`) that\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:44:`/new` and `/reset` would use `bound_acp_or_owner_or_allowlist`.\n/app/docs/experiments/proposals/acp-bound-command-auth.md:77:3. Move `/new` and `/reset` to metadata-driven policy.\n/app/docs/web/tui.md:105:- `/new` or `/reset` (reset the session)\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:129:  - [Do sessions reset automatically if I never send `/new`?](#do-sessions-reset-automatically-if-i-never-send-new)\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1848:Send `/new` or `/reset` as a standalone message. See [Session management](/concepts/session).\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1884:- Use `/compact` before long tasks, and `/new` when switching topics.\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1930:  /new\n/app/docs/help/faq.md:1947:Fix: start a fresh session with `/new` (standalone message).\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:141:    resetTriggers: [\"/new\", \"/reset\"],\n/app/docs/start/openclaw.md:155:- `/new` or `/reset` starts a fresh session for that chat (configurable via `resetTriggers`). If sent alone, the agent replies with a short hello to confirm the reset.\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:707:    \"command:new\",\n/app/docs/tools/plugin.md:713:      description: \"Runs when /new is invoked\",\n/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:103:- `/reset` or `/new [model]` (optional model hint; remainder is passed through)\n/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:124:- `/new <model>` accepts a model alias, `provider/model`, or a provider name (fuzzy match); if no match, the text is treated as the message body.\n/app/docs/tools/acp-agents.md:209:- In bound conversations, `/new` and `/reset` reset the same ACP session key in place.\n/