{"type":"message","id":"19f3fe02","parentId":"39fd4ae4","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:57.819Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering startup message**\n\nI think the startup message might be hardcoded as a default when using `/new` alone. It feels like I might need to override it with a hook, possibly through BOOTSTRAP. The user is looking for a personalized greeting instead of a generic one. It’s likely that after a reset, the assistant generates a default response. I need to figure out how to create a hook to suppress that default hello and inspect the docs for command:new hooks.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa54eec8191bb33df34dc465e5c\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2lqpUMUZL-4J-nBk_vnXRqv78iGmu4TUiaX37ZjrwFha4CnoQimg_1i3rlZGuU9NeFHEuEkL0a1F6UzmrCjGZYJEE_wOyWwI_cfXMPAMFuVU0y-jWuGMdg6feAwvVeievqQzFsdT1gAgvGt9bpSfbv80au7HyUSAZ1yyml2IsbALWQGyRyVGNnOPQtJU_yPNkzNm_Ud-fVfamYZWKqmzM4odaxTmqArLidaG6qyhjPknVDcRTmdKQh6Mfrn269N9rKNDoEMqtwqtGPXfxPciQyDDTOQtRjSTTdlSEwa5RSmZDxDHaRV0itJfbOgjWuS0tHhHpH-IC4rspeqAAYPEK2oM1DqtVvcq8pBuCIvvbby22iJ6qprFKKOoQP0vwqRkGBCpX6LCsPusnG-EmVY8xB83of1odr7q6o1tU9-kpCQqGetTzIyA8Ub0pu6HYpnPuDPTrM08xu52tSzrRgCPNF9lF2Jf4zCdFqm5KviLfzrJ90RS72fUVWvnmOCeM0wapPNW6T_zbbypfkgovdbGHMVpMbXTbr6JgPtctSMCbt8JFvvrNF8d3xQiDJAJQDUil4v3JTyfzBeXwOwgFJKE6yWIYSsgEVk93D--re6QhBIMrqJFTlAUzxvvPPhgpiFFZ6nUTrrakTRctV2ETk6HlAHM4zdYd35laVax8_JHxwSZdlCyatjtGPDfVYrVjR44usUYQ49g2a0f3jrwNjLCfxdzQhg0u_UaDMB6Kh18JHoFRqIHmMa5b0ns7H8dgqCNRIU1b5PuAbSuwo38AmTU5052BTCadEJL550cu7eOBmZaqPdSoNksUw9CalKIK_kJGIkij2_b7bmORLP38fKEnCb202vot1T0NjQFhZ4Asy81us7GbH_NzlqHisq2LzVu0KtKmVvqTwN7MMvCrzOA2kG0VF7wGPtlpI883Y5XDsYG1Kkewa2l-2cpqAGKHM292H5EMeZb-jFf00EBaHIO6f_QvmPJktllfl-lJAfuG-N3DyXxIEI0fXDdQjRgaQeHsrAA_zvOKDfUy7QA-dYowY9BhSpznvT_DYnArVVJ-umj2gq-IM-hf6V3NYji6P5OQk8qH34OjC5WJwqfpZMF7pcVGLiQzozoOlAJnyaEah1A_tQjXVSH7_9YUNuAlQOcRQyah17oPIpQ3WRffyvUjpkHLUJby4-wz228lQWPXEJkcgUfPipgsMFG1C6KI7VKw36zGyOMbqVtBGT2mrs96YP9WI22Z_LZzYpbe7ZCDq7A_8j3FKDR6jpY0qySZUotzIVF6Vb91-VAJHtoDPrhhTgmRhOWFr5Vbx2UYi8VqVQJuV2ordfAM6nnq9cWGt6InPYzE4dhIU3ks8GkfQ696M2Ye8qOus51bHpH5vOWb2zJWv7NHeUhqaROd0Iw44QI2ct3OC3AeSJOd_xZi1x-ivMOvu8TkdsBQy32u9cNqIRqegc=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering startup message**\\n\\nI think the startup message might be hardcoded as a default when using `/new` alone. It feels like I might need to override it with a hook, possibly through BOOTSTRAP. The user is looking for a personalized greeting instead of a generic one. It’s likely that after a reset, the assistant generates a default response. I need to figure out how to create a hook to suppress that default hello and inspect the docs for command:new hooks.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"The docs confirm `/new` sends a built-in confirmation if it’s used by itself, so I’m looking for the supported way to replace that default confirmation instead of fighting it at the prompt layer.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa94c208191a9508ec5fc9bdda7\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qzz9RsUvHcUNS0mr0o7dxRqj|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c61c8191ad51778f0b17d825","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/start/openclaw.md","offset":145,"limit":30},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/start/openclaw.md\",\"offset\":145,\"limit\":30}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uUrzar8YNNdOGGf8pmqvxMhQ|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c62c8191aa8ab3823ee6f12f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md","offset":90,"limit":50},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/tools/slash-commands.md\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":50}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_LPJ0JVVp6Y7fz7Jj5KaTYvxD|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c6308191baeffdf729f4bdb9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md","offset":880,"limit":80},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"/app/docs/automation/hooks.md\",\"offset\":880,\"limit\":80}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":4713,"output":245,"cacheRead":17408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22366,"cost":{"input":0.011782500000000001,"output":0.003675,"cacheRead":0.004352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0198095}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775917732411}}
{"type":"message","id":"f0d00c82","parentId":"19f3fe02","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:57.830Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_qzz9RsUvHcUNS0mr0o7dxRqj|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c61c8191ad51778f0b17d825","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      idleMinutes: 10080,\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Sessions and memory\n\n- Session files: `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/sessions/{{SessionId}}.jsonl`\n- Session metadata (token usage, last route, etc): `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/sessions/sessions.json` (legacy: `~/.openclaw/sessions/sessions.json`)\n- `/new` or `/reset` starts a fresh session for that chat (configurable via `resetTriggers`). If sent alone, the agent replies with a short hello to confirm the reset.\n- `/compact [instructions]` compacts the session context and reports the remaining context budget.\n\n## Heartbeats (proactive mode)\n\nBy default, OpenClaw runs a heartbeat every 30 minutes with the prompt:\n`Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly. Do not infer or repeat old tasks from prior chats. If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.`\nSet `agents.defaults.heartbeat.every: \"0m\"` to disable.\n\n- If `HEARTBEAT.md` exists but is effectively empty (only blank lines and markdown headers like `# Heading`), OpenClaw skips the heartbeat run to save API calls.\n- If the file is missing, the heartbeat still runs and the model decides what to do.\n- If the agent replies with `HEARTBEAT_OK` (optionally with short padding; see `agents.defaults.heartbeat.ackMaxChars`), OpenClaw suppresses outbound delivery for that heartbeat.\n- By default, heartbeat delivery to DM-style `user:<id>` targets is allowed. Set `agents.defaults.heartbeat.directPolicy: \"block\"` to suppress direct-target delivery while keeping heartbeat runs active.\n- Heartbeats run full agent turns — shorter intervals burn more tokens.\n\n```json5\n{\n  agent: {\n    heartbeat: { every: \"30m\" },\n  },\n\n[43 more lines in file. Use offset=175 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917737827}}
{"type":"message","id":"cbe9d75c","parentId":"f0d00c82","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:57.837Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_uUrzar8YNNdOGGf8pmqvxMhQ|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c62c8191aa8ab3823ee6f12f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- `/tell <id|#> <message>` (alias for `/steer`)\n- `/config show|get|set|unset` (persist config to disk, owner-only; requires `commands.config: true`)\n- `/debug show|set|unset|reset` (runtime overrides, owner-only; requires `commands.debug: true`)\n- `/usage off|tokens|full|cost` (per-response usage footer or local cost summary)\n- `/tts off|always|inbound|tagged|status|provider|limit|summary|audio` (control TTS; see [/tts](/tts))\n  - Discord: native command is `/voice` (Discord reserves `/tts`); text `/tts` still works.\n- `/stop`\n- `/restart`\n- `/dock-telegram` (alias: `/dock_telegram`) (switch replies to Telegram)\n- `/dock-discord` (alias: `/dock_discord`) (switch replies to Discord)\n- `/dock-slack` (alias: `/dock_slack`) (switch replies to Slack)\n- `/activation mention|always` (groups only)\n- `/send on|off|inherit` (owner-only)\n- `/reset` or `/new [model]` (optional model hint; remainder is passed through)\n- `/think <off|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh>` (dynamic choices by model/provider; aliases: `/thinking`, `/t`)\n- `/fast status|on|off` (omitting the arg shows the current effective fast-mode state)\n- `/verbose on|full|off` (alias: `/v`)\n- `/reasoning on|off|stream` (alias: `/reason`; when on, sends a separate message prefixed `Reasoning:`; `stream` = Telegram draft only)\n- `/elevated on|off|ask|full` (alias: `/elev`; `full` skips exec approvals)\n- `/exec host=<sandbox|gateway|node> security=<deny|allowlist|full> ask=<off|on-miss|always> node=<id>` (send `/exec` to show current)\n- `/model <name>` (alias: `/models`; or `/<alias>` from `agents.defaults.models.*.alias`)\n- `/queue <mode>` (plus options like `debounce:2s cap:25 drop:summarize`; send `/queue` to see current settings)\n- `/bash <command>` (host-only; alias for `! <command>`; requires `commands.bash: true` + `tools.elevated` allowlists)\n\nText-only:\n\n- `/compact [instructions]` (see [/concepts/compaction](/concepts/compaction))\n- `! <command>` (host-only; one at a time; use `!poll` + `!stop` for long-running jobs)\n- `!poll` (check output / status; accepts optional `sessionId`; `/bash poll` also works)\n- `!stop` (stop the running bash job; accepts optional `sessionId`; `/bash stop` also works)\n\nNotes:\n\n- Commands accept an optional `:` between the command and args (e.g. `/think: high`, `/send: on`, `/help:`).\n- `/new <model>` accepts a model alias, `provider/model`, or a provider name (fuzzy match); if no match, the text is treated as the message body.\n- For full provider usage breakdown, use `openclaw status --usage`.\n- `/allowlist add|remove` requires `commands.config=true` and honors channel `configWrites`.\n- In multi-account channels, config-targeted `/allowlist --account <id>` and `/config set channels.<provider>.accounts.<id>...` also honor the target account's `configWrites`.\n- `/usage` controls the per-response usage footer; `/usage cost` prints a local cost summary from OpenClaw session logs.\n- `/restart` is enabled by default; set `commands.restart: false` to disable it.\n- Discord-only native command: `/vc join|leave|status` controls voice channels (requires `channels.discord.voice` and native commands; not available as text).\n- Discord thread-binding commands (`/focus`, `/unfocus`, `/agents`, `/session idle`, `/session max-age`) require effective thread bindings to be enabled (`session.threadBindings.enabled` and/or `channels.discord.threadBindings.enabled`).\n- ACP command reference and runtime behavior: [ACP Agents](/tools/acp-agents).\n- `/verbose` is meant for debugging and extra visibility; keep it **off** in normal use.\n- `/fast on|off` persists a session override. Use the Sessions UI `inherit` option to clear it and fall back to config defaults.\n- Tool failure summaries are still shown when relevant, but detailed failure text is only included when `/verbose` is `on` or `full`.\n- `/reasoning` (and `/verbose`) are risky in group settings: they may reveal internal reasoning or tool output you did not intend to expose. Prefer leaving them off, especially in group chats.\n- **Fast path:** command-only messages from allowlisted senders are handled immediately (bypass queue + model).\n- **Group mention gating:** command-only messages from allowlisted senders bypass mention requirements.\n- **Inline shortcuts (allowlisted senders only):** certain commands also work when embedded in a normal message and are stripped before the model sees the remaining text.\n\n[87 more lines in file. Use offset=140 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917737835}}
{"type":"message","id":"1f98d73e","parentId":"cbe9d75c","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:28:57.845Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_LPJ0JVVp6Y7fz7Jj5KaTYvxD|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aa9c6308191baeffdf729f4bdb9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    ↓\nCheck eligibility (bins, env, config, os)\n    ↓\nLoad handlers from eligible hooks\n    ↓\nRegister handlers for events\n```\n\n### Event Flow\n\n```\nUser sends /new\n    ↓\nCommand validation\n    ↓\nCreate hook event\n    ↓\nTrigger hook (all registered handlers)\n    ↓\nCommand processing continues\n    ↓\nSession reset\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Hook Not Discovered\n\n1. Check directory structure:\n\n   ```bash\n   ls -la ~/.openclaw/hooks/my-hook/\n   # Should show: HOOK.md, handler.ts\n   ```\n\n2. Verify HOOK.md format:\n\n   ```bash\n   cat ~/.openclaw/hooks/my-hook/HOOK.md\n   # Should have YAML frontmatter with name and metadata\n   ```\n\n3. List all discovered hooks:\n\n   ```bash\n   openclaw hooks list\n   ```\n\n### Hook Not Eligible\n\nCheck requirements:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw hooks info my-hook\n```\n\nLook for missing:\n\n- Binaries (check PATH)\n- Environment variables\n- Config values\n- OS compatibility\n\n### Hook Not Executing\n\n1. Verify hook is enabled:\n\n   ```bash\n   openclaw hooks list\n   # Should show ✓ next to enabled hooks\n   ```\n\n2. Restart your gateway process so hooks reload.\n\n3. Check gateway logs for errors:\n\n   ```bash\n   ./scripts/clawlog.sh | grep hook\n   ```\n\n\n[91 more lines in file. Use offset=960 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775917737840}}
{"type":"message","id":"bea7bfaf","parentId":"1f98d73e","timestamp":"2026-04-11T14:29:04.217Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Exploring API modifications**\n\nI need to figure out how to suppress the built-in confirmation. It might not be possible through hooks, but maybe the hook can send its own message via the API. I think searching for more examples in the hook documentation could help, especially regarding returning modified events. I’ll also take a look at the search handler API to see if there’s a way to cancel this confirmation. Lots to explore here!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aaaacf48191bea2ad5f4d49e282\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2lqtt_hkR3yT2qK2DprEL7vPofulMrDNYSW-WDte4xSNwYshilWa0O9WvWB_5IpOlrjCL6KveJuqoaQHq-k2RUH-neDZ1VIUFS8WSoTL3AQBVk9qB8zea2jIbdNu-sV0Lc5_MO4JpSfv54K70_u8wAgLnQ8ktOD47fq93CyZ6bPxlLzRuSLLSsWGiZRsAZQIGwP9dFBgt-CtuVQVszTNo1QKm3rJih_dfHi24Gg5V9lBeKvox0j3YUUzhxjbl3viPguFD2684_0Fh_hOSsqNVRHmmLMdUdbDUjV5y7sPwpn8puxWiSN6zN2RVt6QX0V5OXhDdSuafzhzKfjbSRrU5SU-okaSK47QIoMdm7iNaF5-WEY1WaTLHVSAcQ3ng-roXXLuYaChwAL4gHI-WrRiv-ihFJNxdK1oPgSqa2ujlxp2g5ZrOvRPqg8Sa0hgPo1NkPrD0-Yzyi3StppVdjbOAG4eoDLQ6W-7fFA8a3ADMOSlnlkMD-f2UyFojdtstQdNho9-NnJC50aAyVg_tE6jzx29cmi9vC0Q8UzwFRUR7SDBVUvGwD12PZT21YNsx2N7phb32hTfNj0oJjUORrytJBscmg17TjLrYdZTj4zWh-d-z8cVgltYMr1n3p4yzwMDFRP6feRsU8Z0wm0akIz1dQJdyuz786tp55LWefeIC0vL2qTEcugxMbwLjeH3uLc4Qe_c9fmBS0Y050bA3-6frOYB4pwcw-C21_uqh18ZHQldOkyqXNfzr9OM5vdv-ybbjk_wdAbP-FKH7BcDw-TJldvpOUdSbgmy2lqPAG3ro6-1Asiu0oU3Pmc-DPQKLigpne_MWf_FJzD3uS2J6tw9SC05noIEEqvaRJd8ZoxzuWfU1gyYFZ3_W8MDG7_63kNMs2v1I2-ca7_QxOPNme8j_YbLXnaq_81T6gnRs4oB4aeqOGtxdi4uvH-kdPkjFgrVPLN7CFMys1c3q3HuQ5rB8XyS7wAAyoOQilmAOi_8MlpDnETpOfDocW9P_ZwoCU_38Sr6Wm4OjgVTshZWtO1AmQN9pU3Ls_Zu9QU7LXFw2q5lZLorKR4ATuzD2FAuRD_6Cjxsb5bR99JTv3wBqm5JKT8I8DAM5OiprMdWQq1xdeAMFm4=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Exploring API modifications**\\n\\nI need to figure out how to suppress the built-in confirmation. It might not be possible through hooks, but maybe the hook can send its own message via the API. I think searching for more examples in the hook documentation could help, especially regarding returning modified events. I’ll also take a look at the search handler API to see if there’s a way to cancel this confirmation. Lots to explore here!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"The built-in `/new` confirmation happens after hooks run, so I need to verify whether hooks can cancel or replace it; otherwise the real fix will be in config rather than prompt files.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5aad1dcc8191b0a265a4b270d1a7\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hkiRDmbabbzNnlpTe6MIptAV|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5ab0270881918ccad3fe6ebea888","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"cancel\\|preventDefault\\|return false\\|suppress\\|short hello\" /app/docs/automation/hooks.md | head -80","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"cancel\\\\|preventDefault\\\\|return false\\\\|suppress\\\\|short hello\\\" /app/docs/automation/hooks.md | head -80\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oNcuXR5RaY3UxEUZBORIgHIY|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5ab0271c8191bb1b8e9d9f758a5c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -R \"short hello to confirm the reset\\|replies with a short hello\" -n /app/docs /app 2>/dev/null | head -50","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":10000},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"grep -R \\\"short hello to confirm the reset\\\\|replies with a short hello\\\" -n /app/docs /app 2>/dev/null | head -50\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":10000}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YV4k2Dtvsf9vQwzOX8G4VzUd|fc_0e24ea3d5e73ae7d0169da5ab027248191811adafced2c6868","name":"exec","arguments":